Interactive USD edits of prims and materials, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

A sphere in front of the camera has its material attribute changed, moves out of the frame and back, and a cube
with a new material is added and then removed, the stage being re-rendered after each edit. The scenario runs with
the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session (as MtoA's usd proxy
shapes), and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image.

Some edits aren't rendered correctly yet by the procedural, they are reported as warnings (known issues in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
